+### Context values and optional targeting keys
+
+Use OpenFeature `Value` primitives, lists and structures for evaluation attributes.
+The provider preserves their JSON types in the native SDK context.
+
+OpenFeature Kotlin requires a non-null string targeting key. To distinguish an
+omitted key from a blank key with this provider, pass `DatadogEvaluationContext`
+through the normal OpenFeature context API:
+
+```kotlin
+import com.datadog.android.flags.openfeature.DatadogEvaluationContext
+import dev.openfeature.kotlin.sdk.OpenFeatureAPI
+import dev.openfeature.kotlin.sdk.Value
+
+val context = DatadogEvaluationContext(
+    targetingKeyOrNull = null,
+    attributes = mapOf("premium" to Value.Boolean(false))
+)
+OpenFeatureAPI.setEvaluationContextAndWait(context)
+```
+
+Null omits the key; an empty string sends a blank key. Existing
+`ImmutableContext` callers keep their existing blank-key behaviour. Other
+providers see a blank key through the required OpenFeature getter, so this
+presence distinction applies to the Datadog provider.
+
